@{ ViewBag.Title = "What's new – EBHockey Plans"; }
@*
    Newest batch at the top. To add the next one, copy a <div class="hp-section"> date heading
    and the panel under it, and leave the older entries below it untouched.
*@
<div class="hp-rail"></div>
<div class="hp-shell">
    <a class="hp-btn hp-btn-quiet hp-btn-sm" style="margin-top:1rem;"
       asp-action="Index">&#8249; All teams</a>

    <h1 class="hp-title">What's new</h1>
    <p class="hp-muted" style="margin-top:0;">
        Changes to this site, newest first. Most of it is for coaches building plans, but there
        are things players and parents will notice too.
    </p>

    <div class="hp-section">3 September 2026</div>

    <div class="hp-panel hp-changelog">
        <p class="hp-changelog-lead">
            <strong>Practice plans can now be built from a drill library.</strong>
            Coaches can keep a library of reusable drills, each with a name, how it's run, tags,
            an approximate run time, up to six pictures and a video link. A plan is then put
            together by picking drills from that library. Uploading a PDF plan still works
            exactly as before, so this is a second way to build a plan and not a replacement.
        </p>

        <h2>Players and parents</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Drill plans open right in the page</strong>, with the pictures and video
                links inline, so there's no PDF to pinch and zoom around on a phone.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The running order is at the top.</strong> Every drill plan starts with a
                summary: each drill, how long it takes, and what the clock should read when it
                starts, counting down from 80:00.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Drills can have more than one picture</strong>, shown in the order the
                coach added them, for a progression that needs a diagram per stage.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>A way to send feedback.</strong> There's a footer on every page now with
                a Contact us link, for anything that looks wrong or anything you'd like added.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Coaches: building drills</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Paste or drag a screenshot straight in.</strong> Clip a diagram out of a
                PDF or a video and paste it onto the drill form. No need to save it as a file
                first.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Approximate run time, totalled across the plan</strong>, so you can see
                whether practice fits the ice time you've booked. Leave it blank if you're not
                sure and the total says how many are unset.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Up to six pictures per drill</strong>, added several at a time and kept
                in order. New pictures add to a drill rather than replacing what's there.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Pictures keep their shape.</strong> Diagrams were being squashed out of
                proportion.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Saving a drill takes you back to the library</strong>, rather than
                leaving you on the form wondering whether it saved.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Coaches: finding things</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Tags are chips now</strong>, added one at a time with suggestions from
                tags the team already uses, each with a small x to remove it. The old single
                comma-separated box is gone.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Search by name as well as by tag</strong>, on both the drill library and
                the plan list. Use either box on its own, or both together to narrow: filter to a
                tag, then search within those results by name.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>A clear banner when a filter is on.</strong> If a list looks short or
                empty, it now tells you which filters are applied and gives you a Clear filters
                button.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Coaches: copying drills between teams</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Copy one drill from its own page</strong>, picking the team to send it
                to. The page also tells you which teams already have it.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Or pick several at once.</strong> Pick drills to copy opens a page where
                you choose the team first, filter by name or tag, and tick what you want.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Nothing gets copied twice, and nothing gets overwritten.</strong> Drills
                the other team already has are marked and can't be ticked, even if they renamed
                their copy. Each team owns its copy, so editing a drill afterwards doesn't change
                theirs.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Copy the whole library at once is still there</strong> for the end of a
                season, and skips anything the other team already has.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Smaller fixes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>There's always a way back to the team list.</strong> An All teams link in
                the menu and in the footer of every page, and signing out of a team now returns
                you here rather than to that team's code box.
            </li>
            <li><strong>This page.</strong> Changes to the site get written up here from now on.</li>
            <li>An Edit plan button at the top of a plan as well as the bottom.</li>
            <li>Adding a drill, or moving one up or down, no longer jumps you to the top of the page.</li>
            <li>Clicking the picture box arms it for a paste instead of opening the file dialog.</li>
            <li>On a plan built from drills the button says Add drills, not Upload plan.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="hp-notice" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
            <strong>Worth knowing about copying drills:</strong> it works between teams you
            manage <em>in the same browser</em>. If you entered one team's manager code on your
            laptop and another team's on your phone, neither offers the other as somewhere to
            copy to. Enter both manager codes in the same browser and they'll show up.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hp-section">2 September 2026</div>

    <div class="hp-panel hp-changelog">
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Practice plans can be tagged.</strong> Coaches can put tags on a plan,
                like backcheck or breakout or PP entry, and then find past plans by tag instead
                of scrolling back through the season.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>A kinder button for parents.</strong> The one that used to read
                &ldquo;I'm a parent, just show me the plans&rdquo; now says
                &ldquo;I am a non-player&rdquo;.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hp-section">1 September 2026</div>

    <div class="hp-panel hp-changelog">
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Team playlist.</strong> A coach can link the team's shared Spotify
                playlist, and it shows as its own green card above the practice plans so players
                can add their songs before practice.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The site is called EBHockey Plans</strong>, in the page heading and the
                browser tab. It used to say Practice Plans.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Teams can be put in order</strong> on the front page, rather than sitting
                in whatever order they were created.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hp-section">25 August 2026</div>

    <div class="hp-panel hp-changelog">
        <p class="hp-changelog-lead">
            <strong>The site went live.</strong> Coaches upload a practice plan as a PDF, players
            and parents open a link and see the videos to watch before practice with the plan
            readable underneath, and everyone gets in with a single team code.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Players pick their name</strong> from the roster, so a coach can see who
                has read each plan.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Each team gets its own colours and logo</strong> throughout, with text
                colours worked out from those colours so they stay readable.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The PDF reader zooms with the + and &minus; buttons</strong> rather than
                pinching, which used to fight the page and trap the plan.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>A coach can swap a plan's PDF</strong> without losing the link already
                sent out or the record of who has read it.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
